  "interpretation": {
    "finding": "With raw-depth, forwarded-depth, and occupancy-cloud harness subscriptions removed, EGO pose receipt still stalled in four recoverable intervals (98 timeout warnings total). During the final interval, EGO last counted pose source stamp 42.704 s while the same forwarded-pose topic was observed through 44.156 s; depth receipts advanced and both message-lost event counters remained zero.",
    "limitations": [
      "One low-load repeat does not establish the underlying DDS reader, executor, or callback cause.",
      "No truth input was used, so target tracking error was not measured against ground truth.",
      "The goal timeout and subsequent quality-gate failure are recorded as separate events; no causal relationship is claimed."
    ],
    "navigation_outcome": "The action goal timed out and did not succeed. Localization later closed on normalized_cost_exceeded. PX4 transitioned through AUTO_LAND, touchdown, and disarm without dropout or GNSS aiding. P5 is not passed.",
    "root_cause": "UNRESOLVED. The low-load repeat strengthens evidence for a gap at the EGO pose message_filters subscription/callback path and reduces the chance that external image/point-cloud observers caused it. Zero RMW message-lost callbacks do not identify whether samples were not taken or callbacks were delayed."
  },
